        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Meqabyan (Ethiopian tradition)</strong> <em>Second Book of Meqabyan (Mäṣḥafä Mäqabyan II)</em> <small>(c. 600 AD)</small><p>EXODUS 20:5-6 THIRD-AND-FOURTH-GENERATION / THOUSANDTH-GENERATION FORGIVENESS-FORMULA — God&#x27;s response-through-the-prophet to Maqabis-of-Moab&#x27;s penitence (vv. 3-10) directly quotes the Decalogue anti-idolatry epigraph: &#x27;I am a jealous God, visiting the iniquity of the fathers upon the children unto the third and fourth generation of them that hate me; but showing mercy unto thousands of them that love me&#x27; (Ex 20:5-6 = Deut 5:9-10). The asymmetric ratio (3-4 generations of curse : 1000 generations of mercy = 1:250+) is the canonical formulation of THE PREPONDERANCE OF DIVINE-MERCY-OVER-WRATH that Meqabyan invokes to justify the Moabite-king&#x27;s eligibility for conversion. The verse functions as the THEOLOGICAL ANCHOR for the Maqabis-of-Moab arc&#x27;s possibility: even the violent-destroyer-of-Jerusalem can be received into covenant under the thousandth-generation-mercy provision. Tewahedo penitential tradition cites 2 Mq 3:9 as the canonical proof-text for unlimited-divine-mercy.</p></aside>',
