        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Meqabyan (Ethiopian tradition)</strong> <em>Second Book of Meqabyan (Mäṣḥafä Mäqabyan II)</em> <small>(c. 600 AD)</small><p>MAQABIS-OF-MOAB EMERGES FROM THE PIT and PROSTRATES AT THE PROPHET&#x27;S FEET — the conversion-arc&#x27;s structural completion (vv. 11-15). The emergence-from-pit echo: Genesis 37:24-28 + 41:14 (Joseph raised from the pit/dungeon to Pharaoh&#x27;s right-hand); Jeremiah 38:6-13 (Jeremiah lifted from the cistern by Ebed-melech the Ethiopian — a textually-charged Tewahedo-favorite passage); Psalm 40:2 (&#x27;he brought me up also out of an horrible pit, out of the miry clay&#x27;); Psalm 88:6 (the prayer-from-the-pit). Prostration-at-the-prophet&#x27;s-feet parallels: 1 Kings 18:7 (Obadiah before Elijah); 2 Kings 4:27 (the Shunammite woman before Elisha); Acts 10:25 (Cornelius before Peter — a CRUCIAL Gentile-converts-to-faith parallel). The verse marks Maqabis&#x27;s RITUAL-RAISING from the death-immersion penance to standing-faith — the standard EOTC baptismal-symbolism (immersion → emergence → standing-in-the-spirit). Tewahedo conversion-rite explicitly draws on this 2 Mq 3:11 emergence-and-prostration sequence.</p></aside>',
