        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Meqabyan (Ethiopian tradition)</strong> <em>Second Book of Meqabyan (Mäṣḥafä Mäqabyan II)</em> <small>(c. 600 AD)</small><p>**JUDGE-PATTERN ROSTER** — JOSHUA + GIDEON + SAMSON + BARAK + DEBORAH + JUDITH catalog (vv. 1-3). The post-conversion 2 Mq Ch 4 develops MAQABIS-OF-MOAB AS DELIVERER-JUDGE-EXEMPLAR — but the catalog is itself DISTINCTIVELY MIXED. Joshua + Gideon + Samson + Barak + Deborah are STANDARD HEBREW-BIBLE JUDGES (Joshua book + Judges 4-16). JUDITH is a DEUTEROCANONICAL-EOTC FIGURE (Book of Judith, in the Septuagint + EOTC broader canon, deliverer of Bethulia from Holofernes by beheading — Judith 13:6-8). The INCLUSION OF JUDITH alongside the canonical-Judges is STRUCTURALLY SIGNIFICANT: it marks Meqabyan as a TEWAHEDO-BROADER-CANON-AWARE text that treats the deuterocanonical-women alongside Hebrew-Bible figures as functionally-equivalent deliverer-exemplars. The roster extends the deliverer-judge typology to the converted-Gentile-king — supporting the seed 4:15 reading of Maqabis-of-Moab as RIGHTEOUS GENTILE CONVERT integrated into the Israelite deliverer-tradition.</p></aside>',
