        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Meqabyan (Ethiopian tradition)</strong> <em>Second Book of Meqabyan (Mäṣḥafä Mäqabyan II)</em> <small>(c. 600 AD)</small><p>OATH-TO-KEEP-THE-SABBATH — Maqabis-of-Moab&#x27;s pivotal Sabbatical commitment (vv. 14-18). The Sabbath-keeping vow is the DIAGNOSTIC-MARK OF GENUINE GENTILE-CONVERSION in Hebrew-Bible and Second-Temple thought: ISAIAH 56:1-8 (&#x27;the sons of the stranger that join themselves to the LORD... every one that keepeth the sabbath from polluting it&#x27;); NEHEMIAH 13:15-22 (Sabbath-trade enforcement); ISAIAH 58:13-14 (Sabbath-honor = heaven&#x27;s-favor); JUBILEES 2:17-33 + 50 (the Sabbath-cosmogony + Jubilees-Sabbath-laws — Tewahedo-canonical Mäṣḥafä Kufāle parallel reading); EXODUS 31:13-17 (Sabbath as covenant-sign). Meqabyan&#x27;s Sabbath-oath has distinctive Maccabean-resonance: 1 MACCABEES 2:32-41 (the LXX-Maccabean Sabbath-fighting controversy and Mattathias&#x27;s ruling); 2 MACCABEES 6:11 (the Sabbath-cave-massacre). The Meqabyan oath functions as the structural-FULL-CONVERSION marker — Maqabis-of-Moab is now covenant-bound under the Sabbath-stipulation that distinguishes Israel from the nations.</p></aside>',
