        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Meqabyan (Ethiopian tradition)</strong> <em>Second Book of Meqabyan (Mäṣḥafä Mäqabyan II)</em> <small>(c. 600 AD)</small><p>OPENS Ch 8: MOTHER&#x27;S-EXHORTATION parallel to 4 Maccabees 15-17. The mother-of-the-five-sons exhorts her sons to martyrdom rather than apostasy. The mother-of-the-Maccabean-martyrs is one of the most theologically-developed female-figures in the Septuagint-deuterocanonical-and-Tewahedo-canonical traditions: 2 MACCABEES 7:20-29 (the canonical brief-version — &#x27;I cannot tell how ye came into my womb... but doubtless the Creator of the world... will also of his own mercy give you breath and life again&#x27;); 4 MACCABEES 15-17 (the philosophical-extended-version — 24 chapters of philosophical praise of the mother&#x27;s rational-faith). Meqabyan&#x27;s distinctive feature: the mother-of-Maqabis-of-Moab&#x27;s-sons is GENTILE (Moabite-converted), inverting the standard-Hebrew-mother model. The exhortation-content parallels the EOTC liturgical-praise of Mary as Mother-of-Martyrs and the Tewahedo Theotokion-tradition. Per Horovitz 1905 + CROSS_REFERENCE_APPENDIX §29: the mother-exhortation passage is among the trilogy&#x27;s strongest structural-parallels to LXX-Maccabean-tradition while remaining narratively-independent of it.</p></aside>',
