        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Meqabyan (Ethiopian tradition)</strong> <em>Second Book of Meqabyan (Mäṣḥafä Mäqabyan II)</em> <small>(c. 600 AD)</small><p>SOULS-RECEIVED-BY-ANGELS — the martyrdom-completion psychopomp moment (vv. 11-15): angels descend, receive-the-souls of the five sons, carry them to the bosom-of-Abraham-Isaac-Jacob (the triple-patriarch destination, paired with 1 Mq 3:38 + seed 2 Mq 2:22 and 1 Mq 2:22). The verse mirrors 1 Mq 3:38 word-for-word in its essential structure — confirming the COMPOSITIONAL-PARITY between the 1 Mq Ch 3-4 martyrdom-cycle and the 2 Mq Ch 6-9 martyrdom-cycle that Horovitz 1905 identified as the TYPOLOGICAL-DOUBLE-MARTYRDOM structural pattern of the trilogy. Biblical parallels: LUKE 16:22 (&#x27;carried by the angels into Abraham&#x27;s bosom&#x27;); APOCALYPSE OF PAUL §§14-18 (soul-at-death narrative); TESTAMENT OF ASHER 6:4-6 (the angelic-psychopomp-of-the-righteous); ACTS OF THOMAS 159-160 (Mygdonia&#x27;s angelic-translation). The verse closes the chapter with the canonical-EOTC angelic-reception formula and prepares for Ch 10&#x27;s POST-MORTEM CRIES.</p></aside>',
