        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Meqabyan (Ethiopian tradition)</strong> <em>Second Book of Meqabyan (Mäṣḥafä Mäqabyan II)</em> <small>(c. 600 AD)</small><p>OPENS Ch 15: RESURRECTION-DOCTRINE INTRODUCTION extending Ch 14&#x27;s anti-sectarian polemic with a positive-systematic exposition. The chapter&#x27;s framing: &#x27;Now hear concerning the resurrection of the dead — how God shall raise them up.&#x27; The doctrinal-exposition genre parallels: 1 CORINTHIANS 15 (Pauline systematic-resurrection-treatise — the canonical-Christian model); WISDOM OF SOLOMON 3:1-9 + 5:15-23 (the righteous-immortality systematic-exposition); 4 MACCABEES 9-18 (the philosophical-soul-treatise embedded in the martyrdom-narrative); ENOCH 22 (the four-chambers-of-Sheol doctrine — γ.4.4 Mäṣḥafä Hēnok parallel). Meqabyan&#x27;s distinctive feature: the resurrection-doctrine exposition is FRAMED AS REVELATION-TO-MAQABIS-OF-MOAB — the converted-Gentile-king receives the doctrinal-instruction directly. This pedagogical-framing makes Maqabis-of-Moab a DOCTRINAL-TYPE for the Gentile-convert who receives full-doctrinal-instruction within Israel&#x27;s covenant-tradition.</p></aside>',
