        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Meqabyan (Ethiopian tradition)</strong> <em>Second Book of Meqabyan (Mäṣḥafä Mäqabyan II)</em> <small>(c. 600 AD)</small><p>OPENS Ch 19: FINAL-ARGUMENTS-FOR-RESURRECTION — the chapter&#x27;s argumentation closes the systematic-treatise begun at Ch 14. The capstone-arguments synthesize: (1) creation-from-nothing (Ch 15:11); (2) elements-reconstituted (seed 14:19); (3) botanical-death-and-rebirth (seed 17:1 + 17:5); (4) Adamic-pairing (18:7 + 18:14); (5) prophetic-witness (Daniel 12 + Isaiah 26 + Ezekiel 37); (6) divine-justice-requires-judgment-of-deeds. The six-fold synthesis parallels the standard-Christian-patristic resurrection-apologetic structure: TERTULLIAN De Resurrectione Carnis §§1-63 (the most-extended Latin-Christian treatment); ORIGEN Contra Celsum 7.32-39 (the body-of-resurrection-debate); JUSTIN MARTYR Dialogue with Trypho 80; ATHENAGORAS De Resurrectione (the second-century systematic-treatise); GREGORY OF NYSSA De Anima et Resurrectione (the Cappadocian-philosophical-treatise). Meqabyan&#x27;s distinctive feature: the six-fold-synthesis is PRESENTED AS REVELATION rather than philosophical-argumentation, preserving the prophetic-revelatory-genre.</p></aside>',
