        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Meqabyan (Ethiopian tradition)</strong> <em>Second Book of Meqabyan (Mäṣḥafä Mäqabyan II)</em> <small>(c. 600 AD)</small><p>JUDGMENT-THRONE FORMULA (vv. 13-18): direct paraphrase of REVELATION 20:11-15 (&#x27;I saw a great white throne, and him that sat on it, from whose face the earth and the heaven fled away; and there was found no place for them. And I saw the dead, small and great, stand before God; and the books were opened: and another book was opened, which is the book of life: and the dead were judged out of those things which were written in the books, according to their works&#x27;). The verse-structure-and-vocabulary correspondence is one of the strongest STRUCTURAL-NT-PARALLEL passages in Meqabyan — paired with mq1 8:22 (seed-buried 1 Cor 15:36-38) + mq1 36:43 (Abraham-believed-God Rom 4 / Jas 2) + mq2 18:14 (1 Cor 15:22 Adamic-pairing) as the FIVE PRIMARY NT-STRUCTURAL-ANCHORS in the trilogy. Per CROSS_REFERENCE_APPENDIX §57: the Meqabyan-Revelation parallel is ONE OF THE TRILOGY&#x27;S TWO STRONGEST APOCALYPTIC-NT echoes (the other being 3 Mq 1:1 messianic-figure + Isaiah 19:18-25 Egypt-rejoices typology). The Tewahedo apocalyptic-canon (Daniel + Revelation + Mäṣḥafä Hēnok + 4 Ezra + Meqabyan) integrates 2 Mq 20:13 into its eschatological-judgment-vision sequence.</p></aside>',
