        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Meqabyan (Ethiopian tradition)</strong> <em>Second Book of Meqabyan (Mäṣḥafä Mäqabyan II)</em> <small>(c. 600 AD)</small><p>**DOUBLE-AMEN BOOK-CLOSING FORMULA** — the closing verse of 2 Meqabyan: &#x27;አሜን፥ አሜን&#x27; (Amen, Amen), the standard EOTC book-closing doxological-formula. The double-amen MIRRORS the IDENTICAL BOOK-CLOSING FORMULA at 1 Mq 36:45 (γ.4.8 seed entry&#x27;s explicit-marker: &#x27;closes with DOUBLE-AMEN (አሜን፥ አሜን) — the standard EOTC book-closing doxological formula marking the decisive end of 1 Meqabyan&#x27;). The 2 Mq double-amen completes the structural-parity between the two book-endings — together establishing the DOUBLE-AMEN as the CHARACTERISTIC MEQABYAN BOOK-CLOSING SIGNATURE across the trilogy. Direct biblical parallels: PSALMS 41:13 + 72:19 + 89:52 (the Psalter book-ending doxologies — three of the five-book Psalter divisions close with Amen-Amen); NEHEMIAH 8:6 (the people&#x27;s response-to-Torah-reading); 1 CHRONICLES 16:36 (David&#x27;s Asaph-psalm closure); REVELATION 1:7 + 22:20 (the Johannine closing-Amen-formula). The Meqabyan double-amen locates the trilogy within the canonical-Hebrew-Bible-and-LXX-Psalter-doxological-tradition + the Tewahedo-EOTC liturgical book-closing convention.</p></aside>',
