        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Meqabyan (Ethiopian tradition)</strong> <em>Second Book of Meqabyan (Mäṣḥafä Mäqabyan II)</em> <small>(c. 600 AD)</small><p>TIER-2 AUDIT INTEGRATION (γ.4.8.F) — APPARATUS-VERIFICATION LEDGER. Per the v3 CC0-translation bundle&#x27;s TIER2_AUDIT.md §1 Summary, the May 2026 Tier-2 library-source verification pass produced these documented outcomes: (1) **1 full verification** (Wright 1877); (2) **1 genuine bibliographic correction** (Cowley year 1971 → 1974b); (3) **1 transcription-artifact cleanup** (&#x27;XXX 1&#x27; dropped); (4) **2 independent corroborations** of core apparatus claims (tripartite structure; Meqabyan-vs-Vulgate distinction); (5) **several refined locators and access-routes** (Senkessar Ṭǝr 21/30 via Budge vol. 2; D&#x27;Abbadie no. 55 items 28-30; Andǝmta Psalter commentary as printed-Amharic-volume rather than manuscript-only). **No claim in the translation body was found to be wrong** — every change is to the apparatus and sources index, not the translation. The v2 SOURCES.md (§1.3 Cowley date; §1.6 Wright fully rewritten; §1.1 + §1.5 Senkessar/Abijā; §3 Abbadie locator; §7 Tier-2 list; §1.7 Andǝmta status) and v2 CROSS_REFERENCE_APPENDIX.md (citations #59 Wright + #60 Cowley; Tier-2 desiderata) incorporate the confirmed corrections. The translation_continuation.md text itself remains the v1 published text — unchanged. This entry serves as the durable Tier-2-audit-ledger anchor within the YHWH v2.4 Meqabyan apparatus, layering onto the 2 Mq 21:10 DOUBLE-AMEN book-closing without disturbing the closed-arc apparatus structure.</p></aside>',
